WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.955
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:08.793
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:14.706
Unit eight: Sports & Hobbies. Today you will say how often you do sports and hobbies.

4
00:00:15.006 --> 00:00:17.867
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.577
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:24.232
Teammate.

7
00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:28.006
Teammate means a person on the same team as you.

8
00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:30.790
My teammates are my best friends.

9
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:33.734
Your turn. Say: Teammate.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.462
Teammate.

11
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:39.009
Coach.

12
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:42.841
Coach means a person who trains a sports team.

13
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.264
Our coach is strict but kind.

14
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.177
Your turn. Say: Coach.

15
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:51.744
Coach.

16
00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:53.717
Practice session.

17
00:00:54.717 --> 00:00:57.541
Practice session means a period of time for training.

18
00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:00.289
We have a practice session on Tuesday.

19
00:01:00.883 --> 00:01:03.803
Your turn. Say: Practice session.

20
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:07.830
Practice session.

21
00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:09.538
Skill.

22
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.490
Skill means an ability you get from practice.

23
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:16.222
Passing is an important skill.

24
00:01:16.817 --> 00:01:19.109
Your turn. Say: Skill.

25
00:01:21.967 --> 00:01:22.956
Skill.

26
00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:24.741
Compete.

27
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.202
Compete means to try to win against others.

28
00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:30.851
We compete against other schools.

29
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.998
Your turn. Say: Compete.

30
00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:37.614
Compete.

31
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:39.537
Championship.

32
00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:43.885
Championship means a big competition to find the best.

33
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:46.344
Our team won the championship!

34
00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.556
Your turn. Say: Championship.

35
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.529
Championship.

36
00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:55.551
Warm-up.

37
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.188
Warm-up means light exercise before sport.

38
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:02.027
Never skip the warm-up.

39
00:02:02.617 --> 00:02:05.582
Your turn. Say: Warm-up.

40
00:02:08.433 --> 00:02:09.864
Warm-up.

41
00:02:10.617 --> 00:02:11.478
Injury.

42
00:02:12.483 --> 00:02:14.413
Injury means damage to your body.

43
00:02:15.017 --> 00:02:16.366
He has a knee injury.

44
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.335
Your turn. Say: Injury.

45
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.259
Injury.

46
00:02:24.017 --> 00:02:25.076
Improve.

47
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:27.920
Improve means to get better.

48
00:02:28.517 --> 00:02:30.389
I want to improve my shooting.

49
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:33.717
Your turn. Say: Improve.

50
00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:37.730
Improve.

51
00:02:38.483 --> 00:02:39.461
Dedicated.

52
00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.657
Dedicated means working very hard for something you care about.

53
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.913
She is a dedicated player.

54
00:02:46.517 --> 00:02:49.099
Your turn. Say: Dedicated.

55
00:02:51.933 --> 00:02:52.865
Dedicated.

56
00:02:53.617 --> 00:02:54.502
Benchwarmer.

57
00:02:55.517 --> 00:02:59.165
Benchwarmer means a player who sits on the bench and rarely plays.

58
00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:01.575
I was a benchwarmer last year.

59
00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:04.371
Your turn. Say: Benchwarmer.

60
00:03:07.233 --> 00:03:08.234
Benchwarmer.

61
00:03:08.983 --> 00:03:09.857
Champion.

62
00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.360
Champion means the winner of a competition.

63
00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.996
She is the school chess champion.

64
00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:19.201
Your turn. Say: Champion.

65
00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.056
Champion.

66
00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:27.622
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:28.483 --> 00:03:30.970
Visal, how often do you practise football?

68
00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:34.303
We usually practise three times a week.

69
00:03:35.417 --> 00:03:36.975
Do you ever miss practice?

70
00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:42.282
I rarely miss it. Our coach always says, 'Be dedicated!'

71
00:03:43.383 --> 00:03:45.278
Do you always play in matches?

72
00:03:46.383 --> 00:03:50.568
Not always. Sometimes I'm a benchwarmer, but I'm improving!

73
00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:53.234
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:54.083 --> 00:03:56.954
Grammar focus: Adverbs of frequency.

75
00:03:57.254 --> 00:03:58.417
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:59.117 --> 00:04:00.861
We always do a warm-up.

77
00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.622
I sometimes play on Sunday.

78
00:04:04.517 --> 00:04:06.412
She rarely misses practice.

79
00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:12.376
Put the adverb before the main verb, but after 'be': I always run. I am always on time.

80
00:04:13.117 --> 00:04:16.419
Be careful! Don't say: I go always to practice.

81
00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.889
Say: I always go to practice.

82
00:04:21.189 --> 00:04:23.002
Put 'always' before the main verb.

83
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.185
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.558
Road to the Championship.

85
00:04:28.858 --> 00:04:32.100
Our coach leads a tough practice session every week.

86
00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:36.075
We always start with a warm-up to avoid injuries.

87
00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:40.471
My teammates and I are dedicated, and we rarely miss training.

88
00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:45.393
I was a benchwarmer last year, but I have improved my skills.

89
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.561
This year, we hope to compete in the championship.

90
00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:54.726
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:55.583 --> 00:04:58.479
She blank misses practice. (almost never)

92
00:04:58.779 --> 00:05:02.584
A, rarely. B, always. C, usually.

93
00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:07.982
The answer is A: rarely.

94
00:05:09.117 --> 00:05:11.882
A person who trains a sports team is a blank.

95
00:05:12.182 --> 00:05:15.557
A, coach. B, teammate. C, champion.

96
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.995
The answer is A: coach.

97
00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.103
Damage to your body is an blank.

98
00:05:24.403 --> 00:05:28.776
A, injury. B, skill. C, warm-up.

99
00:05:32.333 --> 00:05:34.379
The answer is A: injury.

100
00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:38.614
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:42.123
What sport or hobby are you most dedicated to?

102
00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.289
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:52.589 --> 00:05:59.793
I'm most dedicated to badminton. I usually practise four times a week, and I never skip the warm-up.

104
00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.895
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:02.783 --> 00:06:07.282
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and adverbs of frequency.

106
00:06:07.582 --> 00:06:12.068
Today's value is sportsmanship. Play fair and shake hands, win or lose.

107
00:06:12.368 --> 00:06:14.661
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

108
00:06:14.961 --> 00:06:17.532
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

